<title>UK: Deutsche Bank unit ups 30-yr bond to 4.0 bln rand.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank unit ups 30-yr bond to 4.0 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to four billion rand from 3.5 billion rand, lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DEUTSCHE FINANCE NETHERLANDS BV</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  DEUTSCHE BANK AG</p>
<p> AMT   *4.0 BLN RAND  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    27.MAY.27</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  3.00	PAY DATE    27.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.25	LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA1/AAA   DENOMS (K) 5-50   SALE LIMS US/UK/NL/DE/ZA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.10	SELL CONC  0.15	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES     *FIRST LAUNCHED ON 24.APR.97</p>
<p>		INCREASE IS 144A ELIGIBLE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
